{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["עֶגְלֹת — because it is in construct state. עֲגָלוֹת of צב, just as one says מעשרה עשרות one says from עגלה of the two princes: עגלות, and from עֲנָוָה: עַנְוֵי ארץ, and from עֲרָבָה: עַרְבֵי נחל." "צב — like ובצבים ובפרדים. Its interpretation according to its context. And it appears to me: wagons made for traveling in formation and on distant roads."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The examples illustrate nouns that lose their final ה when forming construct or related forms."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:49.315986846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}